sxml xpath - Evaluate an XPath 4.0 expression

Usage: sxml xpath [--context-item=FILE] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... [--method=METHOD] EXPRESSION

Compiles EXPRESSION as XPath 4.0 and writes its result to standard
output by the adaptive serialization method, one item per line, or
by the method --method names. --context-item=FILE parses FILE as the
context item; without it the focus is absent. --param=NAME=VALUE binds
$NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE). fn:doc reads local files only. An
error of the expression is reported on standard error as
expression:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description and exits 1; an
unreadable file exits 3. An EXPRESSION that starts with - must
follow --.

Options:
  -h, --help               Show this help and exit
      --context-item=FILE  XML document to use as the context item; - reads standard input
      --param=NAME=VALUE   Bind $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)
      --method=METHOD      Serialization method of the result (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json; default: adaptive)

Arguments:
  EXPRESSION  XPath 4.0 expression to evaluate

Examples:
  sxml xpath '1 to 3'
  sxml xpath --context-item=book.xml '//title/string()'
  sxml xpath --param=n=5 'xs:integer($n) * 2'
  sxml xpath --method=json 'map { "a": [1, 2] }'
